Consider the following Express application.
```javascript
app.use(function (req, res, next) {
  console.log(req.method, req.url);
  next();
});
function requireLogin(req, res, next) {
  if (!req.session.user) return res.status(401).send("Please log in");
  next();
}
app.get("/dashboard", requireLogin, function (req, res) {
  res.send("Welcome to your dashboard");
});
```
A logged-out user requests `/dashboard`. What happens?

Consider the following script.
```php
<?php
$first = "Web";
$second = "Technologies";
echo $first . " " . $second;
?>
```
What is output, and which operator has been used?

Consider the following script.
```php
<?php
function factorial($n) {
    if ($n <= 1) { return 1; }
    return $n * factorial($n - 1);
}
echo factorial(5);
?>
```
What is echoed, and what role does `$n <= 1` play?
